# Single-page app fallback.
#
# React Router owns /food, /workout, /plan, /progress and /settings, but those
# paths are not files on disk. Without this rule Cloudflare Pages returns its own
# 404 for a refresh or a shared link to any route other than /, and the app never
# boots to handle it.
#
# 200, not 301: serve index.html AT the requested URL rather than redirecting to
# /, so the router still sees the path the visitor asked for.
/*    /index.html   200
